unfold:
Like words that in the silence clearer grow;
As they unfold before thy will to know
Gently withdraw thine eyes--

Morning returns to us ever too soon.
Roses unfold, in their loveliness, all for you;
Blossom the lilies for hope of your glance.

unfair:
His future a dispute;
Unfair an immortality
That leaves this neighbor out.

unfaltering:
No lips to lift a word of praise;
But still, with faith unfaltering,
I live and laugh and love and sing.

All our hopes and fears were centered
'Round his strong, unfaltering hand;
If he failed us we must perish,

unforgiven:
Had bidden him to his bosom once again;
The awful sin remained still unforgiven.
All night a bright and solitary star

unfitted:
And I a pauper go;
Unfitted by an instant's grace
For the contented beggar's face

unfought:
"But ye are soldiers, and can fight,
May win in battles yet unfought;
I have no offering but my life,

unfeared:
Swift squirrels on the pastures took their ease,
With leaping lambs safe from the unfeared knife;
All singing-birds rejoicing in those trees

unforgotten:
I have no words to tell what way we walked.
What unforgotten path now closed and sealed;
I have no words to tell all things we talked,
